CDC growth tables in this directory

Source: CDC, National Center for Health Statistics, 2000 CDC Growth Charts.

The data are available free of charge at https://www.cdc.gov/growthcharts/cdc-data-files.htm
Use of these data does not imply endorsement by CDC, ATSDR, HHS or the United States Government of
this project or of its use of the data.

Values unchanged: each CSV holds the Agemos, L, M and S columns of one CDC file for one sex (Sex 1 =
male, 2 = female), copied character for character by scripts/growth/convert.py. The percentile columns
were dropped and the rows were split into one file per sex; no value was rounded, recomputed or edited.
Each CSV starts with comment lines naming its source file, URL and SHA-256.

CDC's terms for its public-domain material (https://www.cdc.gov/other/agencymaterials.html) ask for
attribution ("Source: CDC"), a no-endorsement disclaimer, no change to the substantive content, and a
statement that the material is available on the agency website at no charge; this file provides them.

